    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a1">

                <pb facs="0206" n="940" xml:id="pg940"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Governor McIntire.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>At the instance of the Italian ambassador at this capital, who learns from press
                    reports of the killing of four It alian laborers at Walsenburg, Colo., I have to
                    request that you inform me as to the truth of these reports. Also as to the
                    present situation in that locality, and the ability of the local authorities to
                    prevent further disorder.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
